    "reasoning": "All 16 mathematical answers agree with their own captured Math Academy worked solutions. No submitted grades are supplied; confirmation rests on the worked solutions. q-124301: coefficient comparison gives a=6, b=-3, c=4, so the sum is 7. q-20963: R2←R2−8R1 yields rows (1,2,-1) and (0,0,0), so x=-1-2y with y arbitrary. q-73740: R2←R2+5R1 gives the same echelon form and solution; the source's omitted comma in its vector notation does not change the answer. q-73750: R2←R2+3R1 yields rows (1,-2,4) and (0,0,0), so x=4+2y with y arbitrary. q-130923: R2←R2+4R1 yields rows (1,-2,-1) and (0,0,3); the contradiction 0=3 proves there is no solution. q-91033: y'=-sin(x) and y''=-cos(x), giving 2sin(x)-cos(x). q-337831: y'=3cos(3x) and y''=-9sin(3x), giving -14sin(3x)+6cos(3x). q-65037: y'=1/x and y''=-1/x², so xy''+2y'=1/x for x>0. q-91045: y'=4x³, y''=12x², and y'''=24x; the cubic terms cancel, leaving 4x⁴. q-337848: y'=2x and y''=2, so D(y)=(x²+1)(2-2x²+5)=(x²+1)(7-2x²). q-338254: y'''=-8cos(2x), so xy y'''+3y=sin(2x)(3-8xcos(2x)). q-130930: the nonzero rows lead in columns 1 and 3. q-130935: they lead in columns 1, 3, and 4. q-35391: pivot columns are 1, 2, 4, and 5, leaving column 3 as the sole non-pivot column. q-130955: pivot columns are 1, 2, and 4, again leaving column 3. q-130962: R2←R2−R1 and R4←R4+2R3 produce leading entries in columns 2, 3, 5, and 6, hence four pivot columns.",
